Verdict: SUPPORTED
Rationale: The claim states that Phil Rudd became the only Australian-born member of AC/DC when the bassist of their third LP left the band, and that the LP was released in Australia and Europe in 1976. The evidence confirms that the third LP, 'Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap,' was released in 1976 in Australia and Europe. It also identifies Cliff Williams as the bassist for the third LP and confirms that Phil Rudd was the only Australian-born member at that time. No contradictions are found, and all material parts of the claim are supported.
